// The trailer, v4 (#1178): Tools/trailer-cut.py Tools/trailer/trailer.json
// The owner's verdict on v3 (2026-11-19): no logo first, a few seconds of action to catch the eye (the neon city's landing behind
// the gun, and the gun firing), then through white into the worlds; one wide shot of each world's space, no bench and no crystal
// close-up, no tour's own cut inside a dissolve; a fade through black into the fast part and into the last shot; hits on the fast
// part's cuts and a whoosh on each world's switch; precise aim as a player who thinks makes a match; "SHOOT. MATCH. BRING IT
// DOWN." word by word as each happens; the last shot slower, without the sea, the city and the storm; and every clip filmed at the
// finest detail (maxdetail), since the aurora's trees popped. After two outside opinions the owner passed on: the calm part near
// 14 s, the end card's wording confident, the opening one run with the first shot early, the laser housing and its net as the
// tension before the fast part, the fast part's lengths varied by whole beats, and the cuts' sounds a frame ahead of the picture.
// Every play "in" was found at 60 frames a second (the size does not matter, the rate does). Camera paths count from a clip's
// window start, a quarter second before its "in" (Tools/trailer/paths).
